WEBVTT

00:00:02.299 --> 00:00:05.660
I exist, yet I remember nothing...

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:12.640
I see that your eyes are just like mine,
young man.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.379
Not who she was...

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.370
Come with me.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.500
I'll take you to a world fitting of you.

00:00:28.149 --> 00:00:30.690
Not who I am...

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.630
(Three Years Later)

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.140
(Wenias Royal Magic Academy)

00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:39.189
There's a summon for him.

00:00:39.259 --> 00:00:40.450
Who's Saybil?

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.649
You know, that gloomy guy who God knows
whatever he's thinking about.

00:00:43.759 --> 00:00:45.200
The headmaster is looking for him?

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.960
What's is this about?

00:00:48.009 --> 00:00:50.619
A summon, huh?
What did he do?

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.420
You know, he has the worst grades, so...

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:57.759
Maybe he's going to be expelled?

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.740
What is it?
What's with all the crowd?

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:04.099
Apparently one student gets summoned
to the headmaster's office.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.750
Summoned?

00:01:05.849 --> 00:01:07.079
Why?

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.730
I dunno, but...

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:12.019
Doesn't the rumours says that
Headmaster Albus is super scary?

00:01:12.019 --> 00:01:14.049
Poor guy.

00:01:15.579 --> 00:01:19.010
Oh, come on out already, Albus!

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.280
Open the door, will you?!

00:01:21.379 --> 00:01:24.700
Surely you're not saying
you can't hear me!

00:01:25.079 --> 00:01:28.650
If that's the case, you're
making me look like a buffoon here!

00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:30.959
That is worse than ignoring me!

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.040
Come on, I know you're in there!

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.349
Umm...

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.560
What, a student of the academy, are you?

00:01:39.739 --> 00:01:43.540
What does a gifted youth
such as you need from me?

00:01:43.599 --> 00:01:46.409
(Worst grade in the whole academy)
Gifted...?

00:01:48.599 --> 00:01:51.400
I'm sure you can see,
but I'm busy here.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.939
Away with you.

00:01:53.219 --> 00:01:55.730
I was summoned by the headmaster.

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:57.049
What...?

00:01:57.379 --> 00:02:00.680
Why, that is wonderful!
Perfect timing!

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.459
I very much welcome your help!

00:02:03.459 --> 00:02:06.459
Come now, open the door at once!

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.199
Umm, but...

00:02:08.349 --> 00:02:10.599
You're not invited, are you?

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:16.819
The headmaster would probably
scold me if I let you in.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.710
A sound argument,
and I always love a sound argument.

00:02:21.919 --> 00:02:23.569
Very well, then.

00:02:24.919 --> 00:02:26.259
If that's the case,

00:02:26.389 --> 00:02:28.159
this is what I'll do!

00:02:30.889 --> 00:02:34.340
Introduce yourself, my lil' Ludens!

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.669
Now, cry in fear!
Beg for your life!

00:02:41.669 --> 00:02:44.360
And now, with her dear
student's life is in danger,

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.620
surely even Albus would...

00:02:46.729 --> 00:02:48.340
Hey!

00:02:48.639 --> 00:02:50.349
Loux Krystas!

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.949
Y-you little...

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:57.110
What are you doing to our student?!

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:03.550
Well, if it isn't some third-rate servant.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.060
Been a while, hasn't it?

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.250
Shut your mouth!

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:09.740
How dare you show your face again?!

00:03:09.919 --> 00:03:12.840
I'm here because I have
a business with Albus.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:16.960
Just go back to the hole
from whence you came!

00:03:17.259 --> 00:03:18.479
No way!

00:03:28.439 --> 00:03:29.659
- Don't touch it!
- Stand back!

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.219
Do you have a deathwish?!

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:37.939
M-my staff!

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.210
Holdem, how dare you?!

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:46.139
How could you kick my sacred
lineage treasure, my dearest Ludens?

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:49.090
Your punishment shall be
nothing less than death!

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.900
Your words are too pretentious.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.960
How could you?!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.050
Why is there so much ruckus, Holdem?

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.699
What is this all about...

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.300
Loux Krystas?!

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.330
How did you get inside
this academy?

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.870
How?

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.979
With my cuteness?

00:04:12.449 --> 00:04:18.680
♫As I walk together with you from here
With these endlessly overflowing emotions♫

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:25.839
♫Those eyes of yours are the only thing shining
the light guiding us to tomorrow's dawn♫

00:04:38.459 --> 00:04:42.230
(The Dawn of the Witch)

00:04:44.269 --> 00:04:50.639
♫Walking alone, searching for
The memories of days past♫

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:56.360
♫I simply held fast to how
Empowering trusting each other is♫

00:04:56.579 --> 00:05:00.670
♫As I stand here, feeling your presence♫

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:04.170
♫That means everything to me♫

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.009
♫That's right, as long as we're together♫

00:05:07.009 --> 00:05:10.579
♫Nobody will ever break us♫

00:05:10.949 --> 00:05:17.000
♫Clad in endless power
This binding miracle guides us♫

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:24.269
♫Both memories of the end and the light of
The beginning keeps this heart aflame♫

00:05:24.339 --> 00:05:30.699
♫As we fired off the dream that was
The single piercing hope♫

00:05:30.839 --> 00:05:37.769
♫We swore a vow upon the bonds of dawn
Shining upon the world♫

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:45.269
Hey now.

00:05:45.269 --> 00:05:47.600
How come I'm the only one
that doesn't get tea, third-rate servant?!

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.560
(Episode 1: The Underachiever)
We don't serve tea to trespassers.

00:05:49.569 --> 00:05:52.389
(and The Witch of the scepter)
How rude! But I want one! And the cakes, too!

00:05:52.389 --> 00:05:54.170
Special training?

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.750
You mean, I'm not getting expelled?

00:05:55.839 --> 00:05:56.899
That's right.

00:05:56.899 --> 00:06:00.839
Even if you stay in this academy,
you wouldn't improve at all.

00:06:00.939 --> 00:06:04.420
That's why, I want you to train
at a different environment.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.410
A different environment?

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:11.689
You know from class that
the Church and the Witches

00:06:11.689 --> 00:06:13.639
were at war until
five years ago, right?

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:14.889
Yes.

00:06:14.889 --> 00:06:17.829
I heard that they still do
witch hunts at the south.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.060
And why do you think that is?

00:06:20.339 --> 00:06:24.519
What is the reason they no longer do
witch hunt here in the Kingdom of Wenias?

00:06:25.389 --> 00:06:29.689
I think the biggest reason would be
the war that happened ten years ago.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:33.329
The evil sorcerer No. 13.

00:06:33.329 --> 00:06:35.040
Ten years ago, that person...

00:06:36.709 --> 00:06:40.420
They spread the teaching of magic
in Wenias Kingdom and started the war.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:43.670
All in order to end
the persecution of witches,

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.600
and create a world for witches.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.720
I see you did your studies.

00:06:49.889 --> 00:06:52.250
Speaking of that sorcerer...

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.889
I'm the one that killed them.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.279
U-um...

00:06:56.279 --> 00:06:59.329
No need to be so tense,
you answered correctly.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:03.009
No. 13's picked the wrong
method to do it,

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.689
but thanks to that war,
magic becomes more commonplace,

00:07:05.689 --> 00:07:10.779
and it changed how
the world views witches.

00:07:11.959 --> 00:07:14.939
It would take decades
to learn sorceries,

00:07:14.939 --> 00:07:18.740
but as long as you have the talent for it,
you can learn magic in a couple years.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.009
No. 13 made the whole world
understand that.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:24.839
That's why I created this academy.

00:07:25.019 --> 00:07:28.040
All to watch the magic
that have spread out.

00:07:28.449 --> 00:07:31.069
It took four years to build the academy,

00:07:31.069 --> 00:07:35.230
but in Wenias Kingdom,
magic has became daily commonplaces.

00:07:35.449 --> 00:07:36.810
But down in south,

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.060
witches and mages are still uncommon

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.259
- and treated differently...
- I told you, bring me tea!

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.069
- Let go of me!
- Cakes, too!

00:07:43.069 --> 00:07:45.689
Holdem! Just bring some tea
to shut her up!

00:07:49.519 --> 00:07:52.040
So, so, so delishus...

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:56.040
So I decided to build a witch village
at the southern region.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.310
A place where witches aren't
treated differently,

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:00.600
but just like normal humans.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:05.420
I want you to help there,
as a mage.

00:08:06.269 --> 00:08:11.300
If in three years, the village inspector
considers the place unsuitable...

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:16.800
Then all of your memories regarding magic
and the magic academy will be sealed.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:18.540
Th-three years...?

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:21.470
Wow, you really thought that out,
didn't you?

00:08:21.649 --> 00:08:24.329
On one hand, you're training your student,

00:08:24.439 --> 00:08:27.649
meanwhile you're prepping
to build your forces in the future.

00:08:28.639 --> 00:08:31.990
Very well, then! I love efficiency.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.320
This task of travelling
the danger to a faraway village,

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.149
I, Loux Krystas, the Dawn Witch
that has lived over 300 years,

00:08:38.149 --> 00:08:40.330
shall accept that duty!

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:44.549
Huh? No, we already have
a guide witch in mind.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.330
Well, that means I get to go home.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:49.440
Huh?

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.690
See, I have a written authorisation here.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:55.840
If my job ever changes,
then I'll gladly go home.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.100
You idiot!

00:09:01.279 --> 00:09:03.679
This is why I hate dealing with witches!

00:09:03.679 --> 00:09:07.970
Every single one of you is selfish,
pleasure-seeking, and unwilling to cooperate!

00:09:08.059 --> 00:09:11.480
Hey, I said I'll do the job, didn't I?

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:15.330
That is, if I'm allowed to read
the Grimoire of Zero,

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:18.639
the very first magic grimoire
in the world.

00:09:18.919 --> 00:09:20.240
Grimoire of Zero?

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:24.330
Do I still have to remind you
that it's a forbidden grimoire?

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.100
You don't have the permission.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:27.100
Hmph.

00:09:27.259 --> 00:09:29.480
I know that it's a dangerous book.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:32.500
That single book can actually
destroy the whole world.

00:09:33.019 --> 00:09:36.360
However, I love not
the suffering of others!

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:40.519
Say what you want, you will never
get any special treatment.

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:42.730
That said...

00:09:43.059 --> 00:09:44.309
I see...

00:09:45.289 --> 00:09:48.700
I can let you meet the author
of the Grimoire of Zero.

00:09:49.009 --> 00:09:52.049
Y-you mean the Mud-Black Witch?!

00:09:52.159 --> 00:09:54.200
Hey, My Lady, that's a bit...

00:09:54.279 --> 00:09:56.620
I can let you meet her,

00:09:56.899 --> 00:10:00.919
but whether she's willing to talk about
magic or not is a different matter.

00:10:01.129 --> 00:10:04.940
There's even a possibility that
you won't recognise her.

00:10:05.809 --> 00:10:09.019
I am Loux Krystas, the Dawn Witch!

00:10:09.019 --> 00:10:13.659
Even if someone hides her from me,
I shall see through their trick!

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:15.409
(Southern Tunnel Entrance
(Witches' gibbet))

00:10:15.419 --> 00:10:17.440
Hey, over here!

00:10:18.129 --> 00:10:19.480
Here!

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:21.590
Phew.

00:10:21.769 --> 00:10:25.399
What, is this the first time you ever
stepped outside the kingdom?

00:10:25.889 --> 00:10:27.559
There you are!

00:10:27.559 --> 00:10:29.600
I made it in time!

00:10:30.429 --> 00:10:32.700
You're going to the training village,
correct?

00:10:32.879 --> 00:10:34.279
My name is Hort.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.970
I'm on the fourth year,
your upperclassmen.

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:38.990
I'll be coming with you.

00:10:39.389 --> 00:10:40.720
But aren't you...

00:10:40.809 --> 00:10:43.820
You're Professor Loux, right?
Nice to meet you!

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.100
"Professor"? I like that!

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.409
I'm not coming with you.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:52.879
I'm used to travel,
so I won't be needing any guide.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:53.970
Kudo.

00:10:54.899 --> 00:10:57.169
Those two are with me,

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:59.549
at least until the training village.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:02.500
You came all the way here
just to inform that?

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.889
Good virtue, I see.

00:11:04.649 --> 00:11:09.049
I-I just thought my grades would be
affected if I left without telling...

00:11:09.129 --> 00:11:11.590
I see, so you're just timid.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:13.730
S-shut it!

00:11:13.899 --> 00:11:15.899
Oh, he's blushing.

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:18.049
No, I was angry!

00:11:18.169 --> 00:11:20.120
Besides, Saybil,

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:25.700
why must we have special training
with a bottom-ranked student like you?

00:11:25.779 --> 00:11:27.210
I agree.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.100
Other than me,
everyone has really good grades.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:33.210
- Kudo, come on.
- Let's just go already.

00:11:34.779 --> 00:11:38.259
If you know this is a mistake,
then go back to the academy already.

00:11:38.429 --> 00:11:42.120
Getting expelled would actually
be good for you.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:44.509
What's with him?

00:11:45.809 --> 00:11:47.019
He might be a beastfallen,

00:11:47.019 --> 00:11:50.830
but can't he just try to be
a little bit nicer?

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.100
I don't think he's not nice.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:57.850
He doesn't have to act differently
just because he's a beastfallen.

00:11:58.049 --> 00:12:03.399
Also, I'm not really worried about him
because he's absolutely bad at lying.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:08.330
You know, you're actually
pretty cool, Sayb.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:11.710
I think I agree with you.

00:12:12.419 --> 00:12:14.269
Come on, it's time to leave.

00:12:14.399 --> 00:12:15.440
Okay!

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:23.769
We need to get through the tunnel
and get on the wagon.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.549
Then we'll get to an inn
before sundown...

00:12:26.929 --> 00:12:28.610
What's wrong, Hort?

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:30.000
Nothing!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.970
- Prof. Loux!
- Huh?

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:33.649
Aren't you hungry?

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.460
There, enjoy it while it's hot.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.080
Prof. Loux?!

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:41.860
Did you just feed your staff?!

00:12:42.059 --> 00:12:44.820
I mean, even a staff
needs some food, right?

00:12:44.929 --> 00:12:46.889
Wha? They don't!

00:12:46.889 --> 00:12:49.370
Or like, is that staff actually...

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.950
The Staff of Ludens.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.289
Just as you feared,
it's the witch eater staff.

00:12:55.629 --> 00:12:56.960
I knew it!

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:01.070
Anybody who touches that gets
their magic sucked and killed, right?

00:13:02.179 --> 00:13:03.549
So that's why...

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:06.559
Did you try to touch it?

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:08.929
I mean, Prof. Loux
was holding it normally.

00:13:09.019 --> 00:13:10.809
Huh, you're right...

00:13:11.429 --> 00:13:15.250
So you won't die from touching it?

00:13:15.419 --> 00:13:17.210
Nah, you'll definitely die.

00:13:18.269 --> 00:13:20.409
It's because I have a pact with it.

00:13:20.409 --> 00:13:24.620
Even if I lose all my magic,
I get to live using Luden's power.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:28.580
Me and my dear Ludens
is pretty much one same being!

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:31.159
Ah, my dearest, lovely Ludens...

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.090
Sayb, that's mine!

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:35.279
Huh?!

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.960
S-sorry...

00:13:38.259 --> 00:13:41.460
I was saving it for last.
Spit it out!

00:13:41.629 --> 00:13:45.360
You'd actually eat something
that was spatted out?

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:48.539
T-that's not the problem here!

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:52.750
Geez! Don't blame me
if you get a stomach ache!

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.620
S-Sayb!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:01.629
I don't think I've ever seen
a motion sickness this so bad.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.940
Here, I'll lend you my favourite
handkerchief.

00:14:05.019 --> 00:14:07.570
T-thank you...

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:12.330
I was totally fine the last time
I rode a wagon, but...

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:15.700
Prof! Sayb's gonna die at this rate!

00:14:15.799 --> 00:14:17.669
Okay, okay!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.980
Coachman, stop the cart!

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:23.830
We're getting off before someone dies.

00:14:32.649 --> 00:14:34.960
This is Solm, right?

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.750
So you already can cast it
without incantation.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.419
You really are the number one
prodigy of the academy.

00:14:40.509 --> 00:14:42.870
Huh? Y-you knew?

00:14:43.159 --> 00:14:45.600
You're pretty famous, after all.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.799
I'm sorry I'm nowhere near as good...

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:52.799
Come on, even I make mistakes
every now and then.

00:14:53.009 --> 00:14:56.269
Your grades are good,
and you're really nice.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.799
You're amazing.

00:14:58.070 --> 00:15:00.850
I'm not really that nice.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.250
I just know how to act good
in front of others.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.090
Say,

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:09.230
here, look at this smile.

00:15:10.169 --> 00:15:11.370
Cute...

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:14.230
Right? You're so honest, Sayb.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:16.480
This smile is my specialty.

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:20.389
People would more easily like you
if you smile, right?

00:15:20.649 --> 00:15:25.850
Before I got into the academy,
I can't even get food if I didn't smile.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:31.840
Most students of the magic academy has
a certain reason why they enrolled, right?

00:15:32.149 --> 00:15:35.649
Especially teen students like us.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:39.090
We all want the power to change.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.960
What about you, Sayb?
You have a reason, too?

00:15:43.269 --> 00:15:44.610
I...

00:15:44.909 --> 00:15:48.210
I don't remember anything
before I enrolled.

00:15:48.279 --> 00:15:49.070
Huh?

00:15:49.179 --> 00:15:51.929
I don't even remember taking
an entrance exam.

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:55.340
If I get expelled, all memories of my life
at the academy would be erased, too.

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:58.480
At that point, I'll be nothing
but an empty shell.

00:15:58.899 --> 00:16:01.889
That's why, I have no choice
but to be a mage.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.850
And yet, I can barely...

00:16:05.299 --> 00:16:08.139
Quite a negative reason, I see.

00:16:08.139 --> 00:16:10.330
That's the only thing you have, huh?

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:11.809
Prof. Loux...

00:16:11.929 --> 00:16:14.580
Uh, Prof, the staff!

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:17.899
Are you using
the Staff of Ludens as a pot?!

00:16:18.009 --> 00:16:20.450
You're being incredibly rude, you know?

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:23.960
I'm just letting deary Ludens carry water.

00:16:24.149 --> 00:16:26.559
So, what were you saying?

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:30.289
Huh? Oh, I...

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:33.379
I can barely use any magic...

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.820
Your magic goes out of control?

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:42.919
Yes. But if I try to control it,
the magic doesn't activate instead.

00:16:43.139 --> 00:16:48.879
I see. I agree with Kudo,
you should give up being a mage.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:54.490
Having a magic go out of control
is the worst situation you could be in.

00:16:54.649 --> 00:16:57.919
But I've been training over and over
for three years,

00:16:57.919 --> 00:16:59.889
and now I could use a couple of magic...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.210
And you're going to train
years after years

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:05.579
just to increase the magic
you can use?

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:07.500
Is that... no good?

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.279
I'm not saying that,

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:13.059
but that's a thornier path
than losing your memory.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.720
Magic is a relatively new art.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:18.170
There will always be those
that fear and hate it.

00:17:18.299 --> 00:17:22.529
If they manage bait you into attacking them
and got civilians involved,

00:17:22.529 --> 00:17:25.210
then the mages' name
will hit rock bottom.

00:17:25.319 --> 00:17:28.900
But if you just let them wail on you,
you'll end up dead either way.

00:17:29.049 --> 00:17:34.779
I believe forgetting everything and
starting a new life is also a valid option.

00:17:35.779 --> 00:17:38.599
Anyway, I believe this is almost cooked.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:44.440
Having a witch eat something cooked
using the witch eater staff...

00:17:44.859 --> 00:17:47.009
Doesn't this feel like cannibalism?

00:17:47.119 --> 00:17:48.400
It's not!

00:17:48.519 --> 00:17:51.750
You made me imagine it, you know!

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:58.339
We found the kids from the magic academy,
just as our insider said.

00:17:58.339 --> 00:18:00.329
They've split into two groups.

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.069
Which one might put up more of a fight?

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:06.240
There's a lizard beastfallen
in one of the groups.

00:18:06.329 --> 00:18:10.420
A beastfallen learning magic?
That's hysterical.

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:14.400
The witches used to hunt them
to use their head as a sacrifice,

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:17.710
and now they want
to use magic instead?

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:19.829
Shall first hunt the one
with the beastfalllen?

00:18:19.829 --> 00:18:21.900
Yeah, let's crush them!

00:18:23.019 --> 00:18:28.250
We have to teach those fools
at Wenias Kingdom a good lesson!

00:18:28.859 --> 00:18:34.400
Peace between the witches
and the church is impossible!

00:18:36.779 --> 00:18:39.970
Call everyone! Lay the traps!

00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:42.569
It's time for lizard hunting!

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:48.230
Good grief.
We went off track for a bit...

00:18:48.599 --> 00:18:50.779
But we managed to get to an inn somehow.

00:18:50.849 --> 00:18:52.920
Sho ghood!

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:55.920
You sure eat a lot, Hort.

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:58.480
No, I'm not!

00:18:58.619 --> 00:19:02.079
Mages are big-eater by default.

00:19:02.299 --> 00:19:07.579
Through eating, they can regain
some of the magic they consumed.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:09.980
But I don't eat that much.

00:19:10.059 --> 00:19:11.819
You're an exception.

00:19:11.819 --> 00:19:14.579
Well, I count too, as a witch
that doesn't possess magic power.

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:18.500
That's why, it's actually pretty common
for a somewhat slender big-eater

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.769
to end up being watched
by the witch hunters.

00:19:22.079 --> 00:19:25.059
Then you should've told me earlier!

00:19:25.619 --> 00:19:28.099
- Dammit, that Kudo.
- You got that right.

00:19:29.009 --> 00:19:30.319
That bastard...

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:33.420
Hey, Saybil. Good timing.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:36.730
You guys were with
the guide professor, right?

00:19:36.839 --> 00:19:39.730
We got attacked by bandits last night.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:42.880
We're even thinking of going
back to the academy.

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:45.519
Did they took your belongings?

00:19:45.519 --> 00:19:46.960
That's not it!

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:50.089
Kudo took the map
and ran on his own!

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.900
Kudo ran by himself? Is that true?

00:19:53.029 --> 00:19:55.400
Huh? Why would we lie?

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.069
He went on his own.

00:19:57.349 --> 00:19:59.490
Well, that's a fishy tale.

00:19:59.869 --> 00:20:05.220
Kudo ran by himself, you two are unharmed,
and you still have your belongings?

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:09.099
Appearances aside,
you two are young boys.

00:20:09.279 --> 00:20:11.599
They can make money
by selling you somewhere.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.299
Normally, you two
would've been the targets.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:19.190
However, as you two are here unscathed,

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.380
that means those bandits
were targeting Kudo.

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:22.990
Why is that?

00:20:23.309 --> 00:20:24.660
Why would I know?

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:28.099
He himself said that
we're just slowing him down.

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:32.490
He also said lowerclassmen that can't
use magic isn't worth protecting.

00:20:32.599 --> 00:20:34.470
I see...

00:20:34.759 --> 00:20:37.039
It's a witch hunt.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.450
Kudo must've realised it
as soon as it happened,

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:46.769
then claimed loudly that
he's the only mage of the group

00:20:46.769 --> 00:20:49.170
so that his friends may escape.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.230
Well, a reckless act.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:55.640
Not exactly something worth praising.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:58.880
Kudo once told me...

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:03.069
He enrolled in the academy
to protect others.

00:21:04.769 --> 00:21:10.119
One time, I had a fallout with the class
and I ended up getting bullied a bit.

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:13.529
Back then, he protected me.

00:21:14.839 --> 00:21:16.829
I'm sure he's not a bad guy.

00:21:18.099 --> 00:21:19.660
I shall go.

00:21:19.779 --> 00:21:24.369
It is my fault that I allowed
Kudo to split up.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:27.619
- I'm coming, too.
- Me too!

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:29.170
That's a no.

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:30.980
If we're really up against a witch hunt,

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:34.099
then having novice mages like you
will only make things worse.

00:21:34.099 --> 00:21:35.200
But...

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:37.140
That's enough of you!

00:21:37.289 --> 00:21:39.809
All of you will stay here.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.190
She left us...

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:45.630
Yeah...

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:48.589
But I can't just sit around
and do nothing.

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:49.720
Yeah.

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:51.660
And so!

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:55.009
We'll use her favourite handkerchief
that she lent you

00:21:55.009 --> 00:21:57.960
when you vomited all over the place

00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:01.940
and use it for divination
to find her location!

00:22:02.119 --> 00:22:03.289
Hort.

00:22:03.559 --> 00:22:06.700
You're way too eager to go
against her words.

00:22:13.049 --> 00:22:18.759
♫I saw an empty dream,
A dream fitting for one such as I♫

00:22:18.759 --> 00:22:23.140
♫How would you decorate
A broken miniature garden?♫

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:24.369
Found her!

00:22:24.380 --> 00:22:27.190
♫With both of my hands full of sand♫

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:31.009
You actually divinated a moving person
with such accuracy.

00:22:31.170 --> 00:22:32.660
You really are amazing.

00:22:32.710 --> 00:22:34.869
♫And always shackled by it♫

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:37.099
But really, those two...

00:22:37.309 --> 00:22:39.190
Searching for Kudo?!

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:40.680
Heck no!

00:22:40.789 --> 00:22:43.720
I'm not gonna do something stupid
and get myself expelled!

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:46.339
Especially not for some
stupid beastfallen!

00:22:47.099 --> 00:22:48.980
They're just the worst!

00:22:49.210 --> 00:22:53.440
I think they would've actually come along
if you asked them with a smile.

00:22:53.619 --> 00:22:58.299
I only show my smile
to those who deserve it.

00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:01.440
But you did smile at me.

00:23:02.539 --> 00:23:08.279
Actually, when I'm with you,
I just end up naturally smiling on my own.

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:11.250
You know, maybe...

00:23:12.079 --> 00:23:15.160
I think I like you quite a bit, Sayb.

00:23:16.049 --> 00:23:17.220
Whaa...?

00:23:17.930 --> 00:23:19.940
Wait, why did that get a "Whaa..."?!

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:22.119
Sorry, I just didn't really expect it.

00:23:22.839 --> 00:23:26.609
No! I mean, I like you as a friend, okay?!

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:29.299
I still count that as unexpected.

00:23:33.230 --> 00:23:34.339
What's wrong?

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:37.009
Sayb, that's...

00:23:45.539 --> 00:23:47.009
- Kudo...!
- Kudo...!

00:23:49.079 --> 00:23:50.809
He really is a lizard...

00:23:50.809 --> 00:23:54.549
Sayb?! This isn't the time
to make jokes!

00:23:55.769 --> 00:23:58.009
Argh, I hate this kind of thing.

00:23:58.009 --> 00:23:59.410
(Next Episode: Don't Call Me a Traitor)
It's a bloody cliffhanger bait to make

00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:02.430
(Next Episode: Don't Call Me a Traitor)
viewers wonders what'll happen next!

00:24:02.430 --> 00:24:04.500
So, what's the next episode, anyway?

00:24:04.609 --> 00:24:06.880
Next episode: "Don't Call Me a Traitor"

00:24:06.970 --> 00:24:09.779
Who's betraying who?!
